From 6ad3152f61db9cc9ea86ce48dc5e665034881395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Talaria <324092415+talaria0101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 12:07:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] add tracing extensions: --json, --report-files,
 --anti-anti-debug, --keep-alive, --packager

Five packager-facing options built on a small per-tcb capture state
(struct tcb extension fields), the staged-output memstream already used
by -z/-Z, the print_fields print path (printpathn, print_sockaddr_data_un),
and the tamper machinery (set_scno(-1) skip + set_success) already
exercised by -e inject=:

* --json: one self-contained JSON object per line per published
  syscall, plus begin/signal/exit/summary events; classic text is
  preserved inside each event's "line" field.
* --report-files[=FILE]: end-of-run report of every absolute path the
  tracees touched (open/exec/stat/unlink/rename/connect/...), with
  per-op counts and outcomes; .so paths marked as libraries;
  missing-display/device hints. Works for static binaries (syscall
  level, not loader level).
* --anti-anti-debug: spoof ptrace(PTRACE_TRACEME) self-checks;
  rewrite TracerPid digits to zeroes in tracee reads of
  /proc/<pid>/status (length- and offset-preserving).
* --keep-alive[=N]: suppress exit_group up to N times per process,
  returning success, to push past early exits.
* --packager: preset wiring the above for AppImage packaging work.

Answers the standing asks in the upstream tracker (structured output:
169, 166, 51, changesets 228/286 unmerged; anti-debug: 227). See
patches/PATCHES.md for the registry and reproduction commands.
