index 57de00d14..1a093ecc7 100644
--- a/doc/strace.1.in
+++ b/doc/strace.1.in
@@ -1891,6 +1891,103 @@ If no suffix is specified, the value defaults to microseconds.
 The described format is used for
 .BR \-O ", " \-\-inject = delay_enter ", and " \-\-inject = delay_exit
 options.
+.SS "Strace\-appimage extension options"
+These options are added by the strace\-appimage patchset for packagers
+and for machine consumption of traces; see the repository README and the
+experiments directory for the rationale, comparisons, and examples.
+.TP
+.BR \-\-json
+Print machine\-readable JSON Lines events instead of the classic trace:
+one self\-contained JSON object per line for every published syscall,
+plus a leading
+.I begin
+event and a trailing
+.I summary
+event.
+Each syscall event carries the pid, the syscall name, the raw argument
+values, the decoded paths, the return value and errno name, the
+duration in microseconds, a wall\-clock timestamp, the resolved path for
+returned file descriptors, the classic strace line verbatim, and any
+extension notes.
+Classic text output is suppressed for syscall lines (it is still
+available inside each event's
+.I line
+field); signal-delivery stops, exits, and kills become their own JSON
+events, so the stream stays line-by-line parseable.
+Diagnostics (attach notices, errors) still go to the standard error
+output: when reading the stream with a parser, write it with
+.B \-o FILE
+(or redirect stderr elsewhere).
+Mutually exclusive with
+.BR \-ff / \-\-output\-separately .
+.TP
+.BI \-\-report\-files [\|=FILE\|]
+At the end of the run, report every path the tracees touched: per path,
+the operations seen (open, exec, stat, unlink, rename, connect, ...) with
+attempt and success counts and the last errno.
+Paths whose basename contains
+.I ".so"
+are marked as libraries, which makes this a drop\-in replacement for the
+.B LD_DEBUG=libs
+scraping that AppImage packaging scripts perform today \(em except it
+also works for static binaries, for paths opened outside the dynamic
+loader, and it needs no post\-processing filters.
+The report is written to FILE, or to the standard error output when no
+FILE is given.
+With
+.BR \-\-json ,
+the report is a single JSON object (type
+.IR file_report )
+instead of a text table.
+.TP
+.B \-\-anti\-anti\-debug
+Counter tracee self\-checks that detect being traced:
+.IP \(bu 4
+ptrace(PTRACE_TRACEME) self\-tests return success instead of EPERM;
+.IP \(bu 4
+reads of
+.I /proc/<pid>/status
+(and
+.IR /proc/self/status ,
+.IR /proc/thread\-self/status )
+have the digits of the
+.I TracerPid
+value rewritten to zeroes in the tracee's buffer, preserving length and
+offsets.
+.IP
+Known limits: timing\-based checks (for example rdtsc around syscalls),
+.I /proc/<pid>/wchan
+(reads as "ptrace_stop" while stopped by the tracer), and
+ptrace(PTRACE_ATTACH) self\-checks (spoofing ATTACH would make the
+caller block in wait(2) forever) are not covered.
+Spoofing TRACEME changes behaviour for tracees that use it
+.I legitimately
+(a debugger run under strace would previously get a clean error and now
+proceeds without its child stopping); do not combine
+.B \-\-anti\-anti\-debug
+with tracing debuggers/profilers that manage children of their own.
+.TP
+.BI \-\-keep\-alive [\|=N\|]
+Suppress execution of
+.IR exit_group " up to " N
+times per process (default 3), returning success to the tracee instead,
+so that programs which give up early (for example when no display is
+present) keep running and reveal more of their syscall behaviour.
+The suppression is visible in the trace (a
+.I keep\-alive
+note on the line, a note field in JSON events).
+Note that a program which has nothing left to execute after its exit
+path may crash or busy\-loop once the budget is exhausted; use the
+.I exit
+of the report to see whether that happened.
+.TP
+.B \-\-packager
+Preset for AppImage/library packaging work: enables
+.B \-\-follow\-forks ,
+.B \-\-decode\-fds = all,
+.BR \-\-report\-files ,
+and
+.BR \-\-keep\-alive =3.
 .SH DIAGNOSTICS
 When
 .I command
